This is the Qualcomm Atheros Powerline Toolkit. It is distributed as 
gzip and bzip2 tarballs that contain complete source code and build
streams for Linux, OpenBSD, MacOSX and Microsoft Windows plus Windows
executable and installation files and documentation in docbook XML, 
HTML, plain text and PDF format. Windows executable and installation 
files are also included individually for experienced users who want 
load and run the tools.

Some documentation and correspondence incorrectly refer to the this
as the Linux Toolkit. That is incorrect bacause information for all 
platforms is distributed in one package. The open source version of
of this toolkit is available from github.com/qca/open-plc-utils.git.

We recommend that you unpack the archive and add docbook/index.html 
and docbook/toolkit.html to your browser favorites then read chapter
1 before attempting to install or use the toolkit. Deveb uwith a web browser 
the read Chapter 1 before attempting to install or use the toolkit 
but the impatient may do the following and survive ...

When you download directly from a respositiory, tarballs and folders 
have no version number. Instead, the version number appears in file
tools/version.h.

TO INSTALL
----------

1. Unpack tarball using "tar -vzxf plc-utils-x.x.x.tar.gz".
2. Enter package folder using "cd plc-utils-x.x.x".
3. Compile and install all tools in /usr/local/bin using "make install". 
4. Compile and install man pages in  /usr/share/man/man7 using "make manuals".
5  Change to the documentation folder using "cd docbook".
6. Add page index.html to your browser favorites.
7. Add page toolkit.html to your browser favorites.

TO UNINSTALL
------------

1. Enter package folder using "cd plc-utils-x.x.x".
2. Remove installed programs using "make uninstall".
3. Remove all package files using "rm -r *".

